1. Bank Management System

About the Project:
The Bank Management System is a Java-based console application developed to
understand the basic operations of a banking system. The project focuses on
implementing core Java concepts through a simple and practical application.

Features:
Create and manage bank accounts
Deposit money
Withdraw money
Check account balance
Perform basic banking operations
Simple menu-driven console interface
Technologies Used
Java
Object-Oriented Programming

What I Learned:
Through this project, I improved my understanding of Java programming,
classes and objects, methods, conditional statements, user input handling,
and basic object-oriented programming concepts.
